PR Title: feat: Add Slug Generator

The Problem Solved: Added a new "URL Slug Generator" tool that converts arbitrary text into SEO-friendly URL slugs and allows users to copy them to their clipboard.

Visuals:
- [Screenshot](/home/jules/verification/screenshots/screenshot.png)
- [Video](/home/jules/verification/videos/7a8dad2fc94887faecb26dd1d549ce47.webm)

Implementation Journey:
- Investigated existing branches to avoid duplicates.
- Invented the Slug Generator feature due to an ambiguous request.
- Implemented `SlugGenerator` React component.
- Wrote and passed Jest tests verifying generation, rendering, and clipboard functionality.
- Integrated component into `src/App.tsx` and `src/components/side-nav.tsx`.
- Wrote Playwright verification script to visually confirm end-to-end functionality.

Tradeoffs & Assumptions:
- Assumption: The user asked for a new feature without specifying one. I generated "Slug Generator" as a net-new tool fitting the app's scope.
- Options explored: 1) Standard text input and readOnly result. 2) Minimalist single-input auto-updating URL bar. 3) Complex drag-and-drop file slugifier.
- Decision: I chose the Standard text input approach because it is the simplest implementation that fits the existing UI paradigm, adhering to the "Simplicity First" protocol.

Testing Instructions:
1. Run `npm start`.
2. Navigate to `http://localhost:3000/quick#slug-generator`.
3. Type a string with spaces and symbols into the input box.
4. Verify the output box instantly shows a hyphenated, lowercase slug.
5. Click "Copy" and paste into a scratchpad to verify clipboard integration.

